{
	title: 'System prompt: who, where, and what changed',
	spec: 'Every provider request carries a system prompt built by the host at request time: a short identity, the date, the session cwd, the model, and one AGENTS.md (else CLAUDE.md) per directory from the nearest Git root down to the cwd, outermost first; outside Git only the cwd\'s (nothing else: there is no home AGENTS.md). The date names the host\'s UTC offset, the clock of the prompt stamps (tasks/nn). Under OAuth, Anthropic\'s fixed Claude Code identity block comes first and the model reads the blocks joined with no separator, so ours must read as a paragraph of its own. Changes the model must know about reach it as <meta> notes in front of the next prompt, like turn ends do (tasks/nn): /cd (new cwd), model switch. Keep the system prompt identical between requests of a session unless its inputs changed, so prompt caching keeps working; test that. Reference: the old SYSTEM.md in the Hal home.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['et'],
	notes: [
		"src/host/system-prompt.ts: systemPrompt.build({ cwd, model, now }) is pure over its inputs (and the AGENTS.md files it reads): identity, <date> (local YYYY-MM-DD, weekday, UTC offset as `UTC+03:00` or `UTC`: changes at midnight, not per request), <cwd>, <model>, then each AGENTS.md as <file path=...>, outermost first. host.runTurn builds it per provider round from sessions.open(id).cwd and the turn's model; synthetic models get none. anthropic.ts puts it after the OAuth identity block with cache_control.",
		'systemPrompt.candidates(cwd) lists the directories, as the old Hal (~/.hal/src/server/runtime/system-prompt.ts): nearest ancestor with .git down to the cwd, else the cwd alone; build reads AGENTS.md, falling back to CLAUDE.md, in each. An earlier version walked from the filesystem root. There is no "home AGENTS.md": an earlier task text invented it, and the user rejected it.',
		'anthropic.ts prefixes our system block with a blank line when the OAuth identity block precedes it: the model saw "...for Claude.You are Hal". The identity text itself must stay exact.',
		'The date line names the UTC offset because a UTC host with a Helsinki user showed [23:01] then [00:36] stamps; the model decided a day had passed and the date was stale. Tests set process.env.TZ at runtime (Bun honors it).',
		"Changes: host.change(id, { cwd?, model? }) saves session meta, broadcasts meta and appends a `change` history record only for values that really changed. Context gained `model` and `setModel` beside setCwd, for /model (task 0x). replay.toMessages collects change records (latest value per key) into <meta> lines after the [HH:MM] and end note of the next prompt; replay.withoutCommands drops them (not a turn: states and recover ignore them), replay.current keeps them across an edit, transcript shows nothing for them (the command's output already says it)."
	]
}
